    yellow is part of the tile content (not overlaid on another color)
    source_tile != destination_tile (src macro position != yellow local position)
  destination:
    determined by yellow pixel's local (row, col) within the source tile
    that local coordinate selects the macro (row, col) of the destination slot
  output: grey separator grid preserved; destination tile gets source tile content; all other tiles cleared to black

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Create 11x11 black grid. Place grey separators at rows/cols {3, 7}.
    2. Pick destination slot (dst_br, dst_bc) uniformly from 0-2.
